<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36974" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pompātĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		pompa, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>showy</i>, <i>pompous</i>, <i>splendid</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">femina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Cult. Fem. 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus vehiculi, for state occasions,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. 20, 12, 3</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pompātĭcē</span></b> , <i>with display</i>, <i>pompously</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Amos, 6, 1</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jul. Vict. Rhet. 10, p. 233: favor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 253, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
